<div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6 col-right">
  <h2>Educators Organizing Online Courses</h2>
  <% published_mesh_number = Media.where(visibility_ssi: 'open', media_type: 'Mesh').count %>
  <% open_download_mesh_number = Media.where(visibility_ssi: 'open', fileset_accessibility: 'open', media_type: 'Mesh').count %>
  <p>
    <%= application_name %> currently has <%= published_mesh_number %> published 3D models, largely biological skeletal material. You can view all of these in your browser with no required software. <%= open_download_mesh_number %> of these media can be freely downloaded for further visualization and measurement. The remaining <%= published_mesh_number - open_download_mesh_number %> media can usually be downloaded after a simple request process. You can use our search page to see all of these published web-viewable 3D models, and you can refine the search further by anatomical element or by genus and species.
  </p>
  <div style="text-align: center; font-weight: 500;">
    <%= link_to 'Search Published 3D Models', main_app.media_search_path('f[human_readable_media_type_sim][]' => 'Mesh') %>
  </div>
</div>